simple linear regression
ŷ = b₀ + b₁X
Breakdown:
ŷ = predicted value (e.g., potato yield)
b₀ = intercept → value when X = 0
(If no fertilizer is used, how many tonnes of potatoes will you still get?)
b₁ = slope → how much Y increases when X increases by 1 unit
(If we add 1 kg of fertilizer, how many more tonnes of potatoes will grow?)
X = input variable (amount of fertilizer)


